# The coexistence case, and the set scenario 2 was written for.
#
# Better Work Tab replaces the Work tab's window through its MainButtonDef. That is the shape of
# defect this mod already met twice: 1.0.1's fix was a tab replacer declaring its own window and
# overriding DoWindowContents without calling base, which made the patched method never run. A
# minimal set cannot see that class of failure at all, because there is nothing to replace the tab.
#
# What this set is really asking: scenarios 2, 3, 7, 7b and 8, which draw or click that window.
# Scenario 6 is the one to read against the minimal report afterwards - its own header says the
# type order may not reach execution once a column has been dragged in a mod like this one, and
# that sentence has never been measured.
#
# TESTING.md scenario 11 documents what Better Work Tab owns and what this mod keeps, and
# Tests/OffGame proves the ordering rule against its real assembly. This set is the part neither
# of those can do: the window, drawn, clicked.
#
# packageId is read from the installed copy's own About.xml, 2026-09-21, not from its Workshop
# title. The staging activates it before Work Studio, which is the order that matters: the button
# patch resolves the Work tab's window class at startup.
#
# packageId                       workshopId   what it is
Coolnether123.BetterWorkTab       3626737803   Better Work Tab, by Coolnether123
#
# The steps scenario 2 clicks with, staged in every pass so the scenarios do not change between them.
nelim.pickletools.clickdiagnostics   path:PickleTools/ClickDiagnostics/Mod
nelim.pickletools.screenshotmode     path:PickleTools/ScreenshotMode/Mod
